          },
          {
            "id": 2767438,
            "level": 1,
            "value": "However, biologists still don't know how serious the threat to their survival is for each individual species. So a body called the Global Marine Species Assessment is now creating a list of endangered species on land so they consider things like the size of the population, how many members of one species there are in a particular place, and then they look at their distribution in geographical terms. Although this is quite difficult when you're looking at fish because they're so mobile. And then thirdly, they calculate the rate at which the decline of the species is happening. So far, only 1,500 species have been assessed, but they want to increase this figure to 20,000.",
            "children": [
              {
                "id": 2767439,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "However, biologists still don't know how serious the threat to their survival is for each individual species.",
                "meta": {
